{"agent":"bugfix1","data":{"by":"bugfix1","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The regression test bypasses `ddflow claim` and calls `W.create` directly; it only asserts `wt.sync_note` exists and the worktree is not mid-merge. A fix could abort the merge and record the note while `ddflow claim` still produces no user-visible warning and returns `broke=[]`, leaving the \"reports nothing\" half of B-claim-sync-conflict-silent unfixed, yet this test would still pass. The test should invoke the actual `claim` command and assert the emitted warning/output.","digest":"dab0ac77ab37c4c8","location":"tests/test_claim_sync_conflict_silent.py:62","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_claim_sync_conflict_silent.py:62"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The test creates task T1 via `run_cli(repo, \"task\", \"add\", \"T1\", \"--title\", \"T1 fixture\", \"--globs\", \"src/\")` without `--phase`, `--needs`, or `--wave`. That violates [r-task-phase-needs-wave], which requires every task to name its phase, dependencies, and wave. If `ddflow task add` enforces that metadata, this setup fails before reaching the conflict scenario; if it does not, the generated task violates the project rule.","digest":"b2eb491fa0cd495f","location":"tests/test_claim_sync_conflict_silent.py:48","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_claim_sync_conflict_silent.py:48"}],"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"output_digest":"9c7556d19554bc30","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-claim-sync-conflict-silent.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261105T210452Z-4370096b.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[2],"status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"e25ebb3fe99f+clean"},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 1 chunk(s) were reviewed (2); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"ebc5e2ddbe7dc4f26b8d1e020","kind":"gate.partial","lamport":143140,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-claim-sync-conflict-silent","ts":"2026-11-05T21:14:42.875388Z"}
